  <prompt>Implement runtime /config.json fetch for external-spa + code-pages per spec.md FR-36 + design.md §7.9 close-pattern. BFF exposes GET /api/config (Anonymous + short-cache) returning the per-env public config bundle (BFF URL, MSAL client ID, tenant ID, feature flags). External-spa + code-pages fetch this at bootstrap instead of relying on the bake-at-build-time pattern. Coordinate with spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r1/r2 on the external-spa impl via /conflict-check before merge.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in .NET 10 Minimal API endpoints, React/Vite bootstrap patterns, BFF /config surface design, and cross-worktree coordination via /conflict-check. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>BFF endpoint GET /api/config returns a public config bundle (BFF URL, MSAL client ID, tenant ID, feature flags — NEVER secrets); external-spa main entry fetches /api/config at bootstrap before rendering; code-pages main.tsx fetches at bootstrap; bake-at-build-time is closed. Unit tests cover happy path + response-shape stability. Integration test with a fresh external-spa bootstrap succeeds.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Per spec.md FR-36 + design.md §7.9: today external-spa + code-pages consume env-config baked at build time (npm run build produces different bundles per env). Every env-config change requires re-build + re-deploy per surface. Runtime /config.json fetch closes the pattern — one build, N envs. The BFF endpoint is Anonymous (public config only, no secrets) + short-cached. Coord with spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r1/r2 required per hot-path overlap.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ConfigEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ConfigEndpoints.Tests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Program.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">external-spa main entry (path TBD via coord with spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r1/r2)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/*/src/main.tsx (per code-page)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="086" status="pending">IaC alignment complete — canonical config keys stable</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-36">SCOPE: /config.json (Anonymous) returns public env-config bundle; consumers fetch at bootstrap; bake-at-build-time closed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §7.9">SCOPE: Endpoint response body includes ONLY public config (BFF URL, MSAL client ID, tenant ID, feature flags); NEVER secrets, KV references, or connection strings.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">SCOPE: If endpoint touches Services/Ai/ paths, use PublicContracts/ facade — MUST NOT inject IActionResolver/IActionRunner directly. Likely no AI touch.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">SCOPE: Register endpoint in BFF with minimal DI impact (single small module).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§10">SCOPE: BFF-touching + external-spa + code-pages surface — /conflict-check before PR (19 active BFF worktrees + external-spa worktrees); publish-size delta per NFR-01.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §4D I1">SCOPE: /config.json returns THE TENANT-SCOPED config for the current env (per host header or configured mapping); does NOT hardcode a default tenant.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-05">SCOPE: /config.json values are backed by IOptions&lt;PublicConfigOptions&gt; classified Tier-1 + validated-on-start per r3 task 061 pattern.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: Coordinate external-spa impl via /conflict-check + explicit coord message with spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r1/r2 worktree owners; do NOT unilaterally edit external-spa without coord.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: Response includes ETag or Cache-Control (short cache: 60s or similar) — reduces load without preventing cache-bust.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Runtime /config.json BFF endpoint + external-spa + code-pages bootstrap migration</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
