    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Anonymous BFF endpoint" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/">Existing Anonymous endpoints (/healthz, /ping) as shape reference.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Code-page bootstrap" location="src/solutions/">Existing main.tsx bootstrap pattern for React SPA in code-page.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Load spec.md FR-36 + §7.9 + this project's CLAUDE.md coordination table.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Coord">Post coord message to spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r1/r2 worktree owners (via /conflict-check + PR mention) describing external-spa touchpoint.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Endpoint design">Design /api/config response schema: bffUrl + msalClientId + tenantId + featureFlags (extensible dict).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Author endpoint">Author Api/ConfigEndpoints.cs — Anonymous, short-cache, IOptions&lt;PublicConfigOptions&gt;.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Options validation">Classify PublicConfigOptions as Tier-1 (per r3 task 061); validate-on-start.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Tests">Author unit tests + response-shape stability test.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Migrate external-spa">Update external-spa main entry to fetch /api/config at bootstrap before MSAL init (coord PR).</step>
    <step order="7" name="Migrate code-pages">Update each src/solutions/*/src/main.tsx to fetch /api/config at bootstrap.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Publish size">Report BFF publish-size delta per NFR-01.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Verify">Deploy BFF; verify external-spa + code-pages bootstrap in dev; grep for hardcoded env-config in consumer bundles — expect zero.</step>
    <step order="10" name="Index update">Update TASK-INDEX.md: task 087 → ✅.</step>
    <step order="11" name="Deviations">Document any deviation in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the coord message to spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r1/r2 surfaces a merge conflict that would delay this task beyond Phase F acceptance, OR if the response schema conflicts with an established external-spa contract, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than unilaterally editing external-spa. Coord is BINDING per hot-path overlap.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Closest neighbor: BFF /healthz + /ping Anonymous endpoints (different concern — liveness vs config). Grep for `/api/config` in src/server/** returns none.</existing>
    <extension>No — /healthz + /ping return terse liveness signals; /api/config returns a structured config bundle with a different shape + caching semantics + response-shape stability contract. Extending /healthz would break its single-purpose semantics.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without /api/config runtime fetch, external-spa + code-pages continue bake-at-build-time: every env-config change requires per-surface re-build + re-deploy (spec.md FR-36 explicitly cites the close-pattern intent). Adding a customer env forces re-build of every consumer. /api/config is the endpoint that breaks that coupling.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test BFF</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Build external-spa + code-pages</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

